#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:5
msgid "バンド構造と状態密度"
msgstr "Band Structure and Density of States"

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:7
msgid ""
"孤立した原子の離散的な準位が、原子を並べるとエネルギーバンドになることを見る。続いて、半導体や絶縁体の "
"価電子帯・伝導帯・バンドギャップを定義する。最後に、許される波数についての和をブリルアンゾーン（BZ）積分に 置き換え、状態数と状態密度を導く。"
msgstr ""
"We examine how the discrete levels of isolated atoms form energy bands "
"when the atoms are brought together. We then define the valence band, "
"conduction band, and band gap in semiconductors and insulators. Finally, "
"we replace the sum over allowed wave vectors with a Brillouin zone (BZ) "
"integral and derive the number of states and the density of states."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:11
msgid ""
"**前提知識**: :ref:`ブロッホの定理と周期境界条件<blochstheorem>`、:ref:`第1ブリルアンゾーン<first-"
"brillouin-zone>`。"
msgstr ""
"**Prerequisites**: :ref:`Bloch’s Theorem and Periodic Boundary Conditions"
" <blochstheorem>` and :ref:`First Brillouin Zone <first-brillouin-zone>`."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:13
msgid "**学習目標**:"
msgstr "**Learning objectives**:"

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:15
msgid "原子軌道の準位からバンドができることと、バンドの幅が軌道間の結びつきで決まることを説明する。"
msgstr ""
"Explain how atomic orbital levels form a band and how coupling between "
"orbitals determines its width."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:16
msgid "価電子帯・伝導帯・バンドギャップを定義する。"
msgstr "Define the valence band, conduction band, and band gap."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:17
msgid "波数の和の積分極限から、1バンド・1スピン・単位胞あたりの状態数が1であることを示し、状態密度を定義する。"
msgstr ""
"Take the integral limit of the sum over wave vectors to show that there "
"is one state per band, per spin, per unit cell, and define the density of"
" states."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:23
msgid "原子軌道からエネルギーバンドへ"
msgstr "From Atomic Orbitals to Energy Bands"

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:25
msgid ""
"孤立した原子では、電子は離散的なエネルギーをもつ原子軌道に入る。同じ原子を 二つ近づけると、対応する軌道の重なりによって二つの準位が生じる。固体を"
" :math:`N` 個の原子で記述し、各原子から一つずつ軌道をとると、同じ考え方で :math:`N` 個の準位ができる。巨視的な固体では "
":math:`N` が非常に大きいので、 準位はある幅をもった範囲に密に並ぶ。この準位の集まりがエネルギーバンドである。"
msgstr ""
"In an isolated atom, electrons occupy atomic orbitals with discrete "
"energies. When two identical atoms are brought close together, overlap "
"between corresponding orbitals produces two levels. If we describe a "
"solid using :math:`N` atoms and take one orbital from each atom, the same"
" reasoning gives :math:`N` levels. In a macroscopic solid, :math:`N` is "
"very large, so the levels are densely spaced over a range of energies. "
"This collection of levels is an energy band."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:31
msgid ""
":numref:`fig-atomic-levels-to-band`\\ では、原子の数が増えると一つの軌道から生じる準位の "
"数が増え、無限鎖ではバンドを連続的に埋める。"
msgstr ""
"In :numref:`fig-atomic-levels-to-band`\\ , increasing the number of atoms"
" increases the number of levels that arise from a single orbital. In an "
"infinite chain, these levels fill the band continuously."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:34
msgid "一つの原子軌道から、原子数1、2、6に対応する1本、2本、6本の準位ができ、無限鎖では連続した帯になる。"
msgstr ""
"One atomic orbital gives rise to one, two, or six levels for one, two, or"
" six atoms, respectively, and to a continuous band in the infinite chain."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:40
msgid ""
"同じ原子を等間隔に並べ、最近接ホッピング :math:`t` のみを含めた模型。 横線は開放端の :math:`N` 原子の鎖の準位 "
":math:`E_j=\\varepsilon_0-2t\\cos\\bigl(j\\pi/(N+1)\\bigr)`\\ "
"（:math:`j=1,\\ldots,N`）、 色をつけた帯は無限鎖の連続バンド "
":math:`E(k)=\\varepsilon_0-2t\\cos ka` を表す。 開放端の鎖の準位は「\\ :ref:`finite-"
"chain`\\ 」（式 :eq:`tb-open-levels`）、無限鎖のバンドは「\\ :ref:`tightbinding`\\ 」（式 "
":eq:`tb-band`）で導く。"
msgstr ""
"A model of equally spaced identical atoms with only nearest-neighbor "
"hopping :math:`t`. For an open-ended chain with :math:`N` atoms, the "
"horizontal lines show the levels "
":math:`E_j=\\varepsilon_0-2t\\cos\\bigl(j\\pi/(N+1)\\bigr)`\\  "
"(:math:`j=1,\\ldots,N`). The shaded region shows the continuous band "
":math:`E(k)=\\varepsilon_0-2t\\cos ka` of an infinite chain. The open-"
"ended chain levels are derived in “\\ :ref:`Finite-Chain Levels and the "
"Finite-Size Gap <finite-chain>`\\ ” (Equation :eq:`tb-open-levels`), and "
"the infinite-chain band is derived in “\\ :ref:`Tight-Binding "
"Approximation <tightbinding>`\\ ” (Equation :eq:`tb-band`)."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:45
msgid ""
"軌道間の結びつきが強いほど、準位の広がりは大きくなる。原子の外殻軌道は、 内殻軌道より隣の原子の軌道と重なりやすい。1次元鎖の\\ "
":ref:`タイト・バインディング模型<tightbinding>`\\ では、 軌道間のホッピングからバンドの形と幅が決まる。"
msgstr ""
"Stronger coupling between orbitals spreads the levels over a wider range."
" Outer-shell atomic orbitals overlap more readily with orbitals on "
"neighboring atoms than core orbitals do. In the \\ :ref:`tight-binding "
"model <tightbinding>`\\  of a one-dimensional chain, hopping between "
"orbitals determines the shape and width of the band."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:55
msgid "|band-gap|"
msgstr "Valence Band, Conduction Band, and Band Gap"

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:57
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"半導体や絶縁体では、絶対零度で満たされた最上部のバンドを価電子帯、その上に ある空のバンドを伝導帯と呼ぶ。価電子帯上端 "
":math:`E_{\\mathrm v}` と伝導帯下端 :math:`E_{\\mathrm c}` のエネルギー差 "
":math:`E_{\\mathrm g}=E_{\\mathrm c}-E_{\\mathrm v}` "
"がバンドギャップである。構造の異なる計算で状態密度を比べるときは、価電子帯上端を :ref:`エネルギーの基準<pdos-energy-"
"alignment>`\\ に揃えることが多い。"
msgstr ""
"In a semiconductor or insulator, the highest filled band at absolute zero"
" is called the valence band, and the empty band above it is called the "
"conduction band. The energy difference between the valence band maximum "
":math:`E_{\\mathrm v}` and the conduction band minimum :math:`E_{\\mathrm"
" c}`, :math:`E_{\\mathrm g}=E_{\\mathrm c}-E_{\\mathrm v}`, is the band "
"gap. When comparing the density of states across calculations for "
"different structures, a common choice is to align the valence band maxima"
" as the :ref:`energy reference <pdos-energy-alignment>`\\ ."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:63
msgid "熱や光で電子を価電子帯から伝導帯へ励起すると、伝導帯に電子、価電子帯に正孔が 生じる。ギャップが大きいほど、同じ温度での熱励起は起こりにくい。"
msgstr ""
"Thermal or optical excitation of an electron from the valence band to the"
" conduction band creates an electron in the conduction band and a hole in"
" the valence band. At a given temperature, thermal excitation is less "
"likely for a larger gap."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:66
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":numref:`fig-band-gap-excitation`\\ では、一つの電子が伝導帯へ移り、価電子帯に空いた 状態が一つ残る。縦の間隔"
" :math:`E_{\\mathrm g}` がバンドギャップである。"
msgstr ""
"In :numref:`fig-band-gap-excitation`\\ , one electron moves into the "
"conduction band, leaving one unoccupied state in the valence band. The "
"vertical separation :math:`E_{\\mathrm g}` is the band gap."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:69
msgid "価電子帯の頂点Evから伝導帯の底Ecへの励起。価電子帯の白丸は正孔、伝導帯の塗った丸は励起された電子を示す。"
msgstr ""
"Excitation from the valence band maximum Ev to the conduction band "
"minimum Ec. The open circle in the valence band marks a hole, and the "
"filled circle in the conduction band marks the excited electron."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:75
msgid "価電子帯上端と伝導帯下端が同じ波数にある場合の模式図。 茶色の矢印はバンド端間の励起、塗りつぶした丸は電子、白抜きの丸は正孔を表す。"
msgstr ""
"Schematic for a valence band maximum and conduction band minimum at the "
"same wave number. The brown arrow marks excitation between the band "
"edges, the filled circle represents an electron, and the open circle "
"represents a hole."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:78
msgid ""
"熱平衡での電子状態の占有数は\\ :ref:`フェルミ–ディラック分布<fermi-dirac-distribution>`\\ に従う。 "
"励起された電子と正孔は電流を運び、その密度と移動度が\\ :ref:`半導体の電気伝導率<semiconductor-"
"conductivity>`\\ を決める。"
msgstr ""
"At thermal equilibrium, the occupation numbers of electronic states "
"follow the \\ :ref:`Fermi–Dirac distribution <fermi-dirac-"
"distribution>`\\ . Excited electrons and holes carry current, and their "
"densities and mobilities determine the \\ :ref:`electrical conductivity "
"of a semiconductor <semiconductor-conductivity>`\\ ."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:85
msgid "状態の和とBZ積分"
msgstr "Sum over States and Brillouin Zone Integration"

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:87
msgid ""
"単位胞を :math:`N` 個並べて\\ :ref:`周期境界条件<pbc-allowed-wavevectors>`\\ を課すと、式 :eq"
":`pbc-allowed` の :math:`N` 個の波数が許され、第1ブリルアンゾーンの中に一様に分布する。波数の関数 "
":math:`A(\\boldsymbol k)` を 許される波数について足し、単位胞の数で割った平均を :math:`\\bar "
"A=\\frac1N\\sum_{\\boldsymbol k}A(\\boldsymbol k)` とする。 許される波数は、BZの体積 "
":math:`\\Omega_{\\mathrm{BZ}}`\\ （式 :eq:`OmegaBZ`）を :math:`N` "
"等分した体積ごとに1点ずつ あるので、:math:`N\\to\\infty` では和を積分に置き換えられ "
"（:math:`\\sum_{\\boldsymbol "
"k}\\to(N/\\Omega_\\mathrm{BZ})\\int_\\mathrm{BZ}\\mathrm d\\boldsymbol "
"k`\\ ）、"
msgstr ""
"Arranging :math:`N` unit cells and imposing \\ :ref:`periodic boundary "
"conditions <pbc-allowed-wavevectors>`\\  gives the allowed wave vectors "
"in Equation :eq:`pbc-allowed`. These :math:`N` vectors are uniformly "
"distributed in the first Brillouin zone. Averaging the function "
":math:`A(\\boldsymbol k)` over the allowed wave vectors means dividing "
"the sum by the number of unit cells, giving :math:`\\bar "
"A=\\frac1N\\sum_{\\boldsymbol k}A(\\boldsymbol k)`. The BZ volume "
":math:`\\Omega_{\\mathrm{BZ}}`\\  (Equation :eq:`OmegaBZ`) contains one "
"allowed wave vector in each of its :math:`N` equal subdivisions. In the "
"limit :math:`N\\to\\infty`, the integral replaces the sum "
"(:math:`\\sum_{\\boldsymbol "
"k}\\to(N/\\Omega_\\mathrm{BZ})\\int_\\mathrm{BZ}\\mathrm d\\boldsymbol "
"k`\\ ), giving"

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:94
msgid ""
"\\bar A=\\frac{1}{\\Omega_\\mathrm{BZ}}\\int_\\mathrm{BZ}A(\\boldsymbol "
"k)\\,\\mathrm d\\boldsymbol k"
msgstr ""
"\\bar A=\\frac{1}{\\Omega_\\mathrm{BZ}}\\int_\\mathrm{BZ}A(\\boldsymbol "
"k)\\,\\mathrm d\\boldsymbol k"

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:99
msgid ""
"となる。巨視的な結晶では :math:`N` が非常に大きいので、この置き換えが使える。数値計算で積分を有限個の波数の和で "
"近似するときの誤差は、「\\ :ref:`kpoint_sampling`\\ 」で扱う。"
msgstr ""
"The replacement by an integral applies to macroscopic crystals because "
":math:`N` is very large. “\\ :ref:`k-Point Meshes and Integration Error "
"<kpoint_sampling>`\\ ” discusses the error when a numerical calculation "
"approximates the integral by a sum over finitely many wave vectors."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:106
msgid "状態数と状態密度（DOS）"
msgstr "Number of States and Density of States (DOS)"

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:108
msgid ""
"1バンド・1スピンについて、エネルギー :math:`E` 以下にある状態数を単位胞あたりで 数える。バンドのエネルギーを "
":math:`\\varepsilon(\\boldsymbol k)` とし、式 :eq:`kps-integral` の "
":math:`A(\\boldsymbol k)` に階段関数 "
":math:`\\Theta(E-\\varepsilon(\\boldsymbol k))` を選ぶと、"
msgstr ""
"For one band and one spin, we count the states per unit cell at or below "
"energy :math:`E`. Let :math:`\\varepsilon(\\boldsymbol k)` be the band "
"energy. In Equation :eq:`kps-integral`, choosing the function "
":math:`A(\\boldsymbol k)` to be the step function "
":math:`\\Theta(E-\\varepsilon(\\boldsymbol k))` gives"

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:112
msgid ""
"n(E)=\\frac{1}{\\Omega_{\\mathrm{BZ}}}\n"
"     \\int_{\\mathrm{BZ}}\\Theta(E-\\varepsilon(\\boldsymbol "
"k))\\,\\mathrm d\\boldsymbol k"
msgstr ""
"n(E)=\\frac{1}{\\Omega_{\\mathrm{BZ}}}\n"
"     \\int_{\\mathrm{BZ}}\\Theta(E-\\varepsilon(\\boldsymbol "
"k))\\,\\mathrm d\\boldsymbol k"

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:118
msgid ""
"となる。:math:`\\Theta` は単位ステップ関数である。すべての波数で :math:`\\varepsilon(\\boldsymbol"
" k)<E` なら、積分は :math:`\\Omega_{\\mathrm{BZ}}` "
"になり、単位胞あたりの状態数は1になる。これは、1本のバンドに1スピンあたり単位胞の数 :math:`N` と同じ数の 状態がある（\\ "
":ref:`独立な波数の個数<pbc-wavevector-count>`）ことに対応する。"
msgstr ""
"Here :math:`\\Theta` is the unit step function. If "
":math:`\\varepsilon(\\boldsymbol k)<E` for every wave vector, the "
"integral equals :math:`\\Omega_{\\mathrm{BZ}}` and the number of states "
"per unit cell is one. This corresponds to having as many states per spin "
"in one band as there are unit cells :math:`N` (see \\ :ref:`the number of"
" independent wave vectors <pbc-wavevector-count>`)."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:123
msgid "状態密度（density of states, DOS）は、単位エネルギー幅あたりの状態数である。 上の状態数をエネルギーで微分して求める。"
msgstr ""
"The density of states (DOS) is the number of states per unit energy. We "
"obtain it by differentiating the cumulative state count with respect to "
"energy."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:126
msgid ""
"\\rho(E)=\\frac{\\mathrm dn(E)}{\\mathrm dE}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\Omega_{\\mathrm{BZ}}}\n"
" \\int_{\\mathrm{BZ}}\\delta(E-\\varepsilon(\\boldsymbol k))\\,\\mathrm "
"d\\boldsymbol k"
msgstr ""
"\\rho(E)=\\frac{\\mathrm dn(E)}{\\mathrm dE}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\Omega_{\\mathrm{BZ}}}\n"
" \\int_{\\mathrm{BZ}}\\delta(E-\\varepsilon(\\boldsymbol k))\\,\\mathrm "
"d\\boldsymbol k"

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:133
msgid ""
"ここで :math:`\\delta` はディラックのデルタ関数である。式 :eq:`rho(E)` の :math:`\\rho(E)` "
"は1バンド・1スピン・単位胞あたりの状態密度である。 複数のバンドやスピンを扱うときは、それぞれの寄与を足す。"
msgstr ""
"Here :math:`\\delta` is the Dirac delta function. In Equation "
":eq:`rho(E)`, :math:`\\rho(E)` gives the density of states per band, per "
"spin, per unit cell. For multiple bands or spins, add their "
"contributions."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:137
msgid ""
":numref:`fig-band-state-count-and-dos`\\ では、累積状態数の曲線が急なところほど "
"状態密度が大きい。バンドの全状態を数え終えると、累積状態数は1になる。"
msgstr ""
"In :numref:`fig-band-state-count-and-dos`\\ , the density of states is "
"larger where the cumulative state count rises more steeply. Once all "
"states in the band have been counted, the cumulative count is one."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:140
msgid "一次元バンドの累積状態数がバンドの下端で0から増え、上端で1に達する。状態密度はバンドの両端の内側で大きく、外ではゼロ。"
msgstr ""
"The cumulative state count for a one-dimensional band rises from zero at "
"the lower band edge to one at the upper edge. The density of states is "
"large just inside both edges and zero outside the band."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:146
msgid ""
"一次元バンド :math:`\\varepsilon(k)=\\varepsilon_0-2t\\cos ka`\\ "
"（最近接ホッピングだけのタイト・バインディング模型、 式 :eq:`tb-band`）について、1スピン・単位胞あたりの累積状態数 "
":math:`n(E)` とその傾き :math:`\\rho(E)` を示す。縦の破線はバンド端で、 "
"下段の曲線はバンド端へ内側から近づくと発散する。"
msgstr ""
"For the one-dimensional band "
":math:`\\varepsilon(k)=\\varepsilon_0-2t\\cos ka`\\  (the tight-binding "
"model with only nearest-neighbor hopping, Equation :eq:`tb-band`), the "
"plots show the cumulative state count :math:`n(E)` and its slope "
":math:`\\rho(E)` per spin and per unit cell. The vertical dashed lines "
"mark the band edges. The lower curve diverges as the energy approaches "
"either edge from inside the band."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:151
msgid ""
":ref:`フェルミ–ディラック分布<fermi-dirac-distribution>` :math:`f(E)` は、エネルギー "
":math:`E` の 1状態に電子が入る平均占有数である。:math:`f(E)\\rho(E)` は占有された状態の "
"エネルギーあたりの密度を与える。これをエネルギーで積分すると、同じ規格化での電子数 が得られる。数値計算では、有限個の\\ "
":ref:`k点のメッシュ<kpoint-meshes>`\\ を使い、BZ積分を和で近似する。 状態密度を原子や軌道ごとに分けたものを\\ "
":ref:`射影状態密度<projected-dos>`\\ と呼ぶ。"
msgstr ""
"The :ref:`Fermi–Dirac distribution <fermi-dirac-distribution>` "
":math:`f(E)` gives the mean electron occupation number of a state at "
"energy :math:`E`. The product :math:`f(E)\\rho(E)` gives the density of "
"occupied states per unit energy. Integrating it over energy gives the "
"electron count with the same normalization. Numerical calculations use a "
"finite \\ :ref:`k-point mesh <kpoint-meshes>`\\  to approximate the BZ "
"integral with a sum. Resolving the density of states into contributions "
"from individual atoms or orbitals gives the \\ :ref:`projected density of"
" states <projected-dos>`\\ ."

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:161
msgid "参考文献"
msgstr "References"

#: ../../solid/bandstructure.rst:163
msgid ""
"MIT Materials Science, `Lecture 7 "
"<https://wikis.mit.edu/confluence/display/MSEDG/Lecture%2B7>`_."
msgstr ""
"MIT Materials Science, `Lecture 7 "
"<https://wikis.mit.edu/confluence/display/MSEDG/Lecture%2B7>`_."

